<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n55949" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατηφ-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with downcast eyes,
				downcast</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατηφέες ἐσσόμεθ᾽ αἰεί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					24.432
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Att.</u>
				13.42.1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν μὲν κατηφῆ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					881
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ὄμμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Heracl.</u>
					633
				</span></i>
			 (but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ὀφθαλμοί</span>
			<i>sunken</i> eyes, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Epid.</u>
				7.25
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. καὶ ὑπεραύστηρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>POxy.</u>
					471.92
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>; of animals, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ ἵπποι ὅταν ἀποκείρωνται, γίνονται
					κατηφέστεραι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					572b9
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Phgn.</u>
					808a10
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				807b12
			</span></i>: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ἄμπελος</span>
			<i>drooping</i> in sorrow, <i><span class="en">
				Him.
				<u>Or.</u>
				9.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<i>dim, obscure</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νύξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.658
				</span></i>
			 (Paul. Sil.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χωρίον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					5.110
				</span></i>
			; of colour, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ὁ λίθος καὶ μέλας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VS</u>
					2.1.8
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Him.
				<u>Ecl.</u>
				12.7
			</span></i>.</div>
